' 1. Proxy startup
' The reference for this protocol. The pseudo code in 1-proxy-startup.md
' details each numbered step.

@startuml proxy-startup

skinparam style strictuml
!pragma teoz true

actor "operator" as Op

box "Files" #LightBlue
database "settings" as Settings
database "secrets" as Secrets
end box

box "Tally proxy" #LightBlue
participant "proxy" as Proxy
participant "writer" as Writer
database "log" as Log
end box

box "Sandbox" #LightBlue
collections "programs" as Programs
end box

note over Proxy
given the paths of the settings and secrets files
end note

note over Proxy, Log
if a line can't be written:
the proxy stops (see 2)
end note

Op -> Proxy : start, with both paths

rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
  1. load the settings and the secrets
end rnote

Proxy -> Settings : read
Proxy -> Secrets : read

rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
  2. check them
end rnote

rnote over Proxy #ffffff
  // <latex>\scriptstyle H</latex> the listed hosts, <latex>\scriptstyle K</latex> the keys, <latex>\scriptstyle S</latex> the secrets by key name,
  // <latex>\scriptstyle \mathcal{P}</latex> the placeholder shape, <latex>\scriptstyle D</latex> the headers the proxy drops, writes, or reads for framing,
  // <latex>\scriptstyle \mathcal{A}</latex> visible ASCII without space (a secret's length is bounded),
  // <latex>\scriptstyle n(h)</latex> the host <latex>\scriptstyle h</latex> normalized to host:port by the Parser's rule (<latex>\scriptstyle \bot</latex> if it refuses <latex>\scriptstyle h</latex>)
  <latex>\scriptstyle \mathtt{ok} \iff \begin{array}{l} \forall h \in H,\ n(h) \neq \bot \cr \wedge\ |n(H)| = |H| \cr \wedge\ \forall k \in K,\ n(k.\mathtt{host}) \in n(H) \cr \wedge\ \forall k \in K,\ k.\mathtt{placeholder} \in \mathcal{P} \cr \wedge\ |\{k.\mathtt{placeholder} \mid k \in K\}| = |K| \cr \wedge\ \forall k \in K,\ k.\mathtt{header} \notin D \cr \wedge\ \mathrm{dom}(S) = \{k.\mathtt{name} \mid k \in K\} \cr \wedge\ \forall s \in \mathrm{ran}(S),\ s \in \mathcal{A}^{+} \end{array}</latex>
end rnote

alt if a file can't be read or parsed, or <latex>\neg\,\mathtt{ok}</latex>

  Proxy --> Op : why, then exit

else

  rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
    3. prepare the start line
  end rnote

  rnote over Proxy #ffffff
    <latex>\scriptstyle \mathtt{settings\_sha256} = \mathrm{SHA256}(\text{settings file}), \quad \mathtt{run} \leftarrow \text{random}</latex>
  end rnote

  rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
    4. create this run's log file
  end rnote

  ref over Proxy, Writer, Log : call 2. start the writer, log the start line, wait until on disk

  note right of Writer
    nothing listens
    before this answer
  end note

  rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
    5. listen
  end rnote

  group while no shutdown signal, and the log works

    Programs o-> Proxy : connect

    ref over Proxy, Programs : call 4. one program connection

  end

  Op -> Proxy : SIGTERM or Ctrl-C

  rnote over Proxy #d1d5ef
    6. shut down: stop accepting, set shutdown,
    then cut_off after a time limit (see 4)
  end rnote

  ref over Proxy, Writer, Log : call 2. log the stop line, after the queued ones, wait until on disk

  Proxy --> Op : exit

end

@enduml
